  "environment_caveats": [
    "Audited the apex production origin (https://purocleaneastlasvegas.com). clients/puroclean-east-las-vegas.json has apex_cutover=null, but the apex serves 200 with no x-robots-tag and the 2026-08-27 baseline was also taken on the apex, so the apex was used for month-over-month comparability. The staging noindex correction in Step 4 does not apply and SEO counts toward the verdict.",
    "clients/puroclean-east-las-vegas.json has status=\"live\", not \"active\". build_status=pushed_main and the apex origin serves 200, so the audit proceeded (same as the prior run).",
    "Canonical scoring is DESKTOP (formFactor=desktop), recorded in audit_form_factor. The run called the DataForSEO REST endpoint on_page/lighthouse/live/json directly; a supplementary mobile pass (for_mobile=true) is stored per-URL under .mobile and in site_rollup.avg_scores_mobile. Desktop remains canonical for month-over-month comparability.",
    "lighthouse_issues lists every scored audit below 0.9 (max 8 per URL) rather than a top-5 cap, so that new/resolved issue detection is not distorted by the cap. Detail extracted from the full Lighthouse JSON on disk.",
    "Severity mapping for Lighthouse issues (unchanged from prior run): color-contrast = high; any other audit scoring 0 = medium; audits scoring 0.5 = low. Only on-page high/medium issues drive the verdict; Lighthouse issues drive it via category scores.",
    "DataForSEO check has_micromarkup_errors is no longer raised on any audited URL (was 5 of 6 in August). However, Organization/LocalBusiness foundingDate is still emitted as an empty string (\"\") in the JSON-LD (verified by curl on /). There is no DataForSEO or Lighthouse check ID for this, so it is carried in recommendations, not onpage_issues[].",
    "DataForSEO passes (is_https, canonical, has_html_doctype, seo_friendly_url*) are not recorded as issues. no_image_title is excluded: the img title attribute is not an SEO requirement and Lighthouse image-alt passes on every page.",
    "The 'frame' check on /service-areas/henderson-nv/ is the lazy-loaded Google Maps embed. It is intentional and recorded as low severity.",
    "Word counts meet url-plan target_word_count on all 6 URLs; titles 48-63 chars, meta descriptions 99-143 chars, exactly one H1, self-referencing canonical, no broken links or resources on any URL.",
    "INP is null on every URL: interaction-to-next-paint is a field metric and is not produced by a Lighthouse lab run.",
    "Raw responses were written to a dedicated scratch directory (/tmp/rank-ai-audit/pcelv/) to avoid collision with other clients' files in /tmp/rank-ai-audit/raw; every file used was verified to resolve to purocleaneastlasvegas.com.",
    "Prior (2026-08-27) run capped lighthouse_issues at 5 per URL. On the home page the prior list already reached low-severity items, so unused-javascript (medium) and forced-reflow-insight (medium) are genuinely new there. On the other 5 URLs, 'new' cache-insight (low) entries may be an artifact of the prior cap rather than a real change; unused-javascript is attributed to the Google tag (gtag/js?id=G-M4N5NVD0WN, ~69 KiB unused of ~156 KiB) on every page and is treated as new site-wide.",
    "Supplementary mobile averages dropped from 94.7 to 87.7 performance (mobile LCP now 2.5-4.1s vs 2.6-3.4s in August). Mobile is not canonical and does not drive the verdict, but the drop coincides with the new gtag.js payload and is called out in the report."
